## What Problem This Solves

`normalizeCliContextValue` (cli-output.ts) and `formatSkillExperienceReviewTranscript` (experience-review-prompt.ts) use raw `.slice(0, N)` / `.slice(-N)` to truncate user-visible strings. When a truncation boundary falls inside a UTF-16 surrogate pair (e.g. emoji), the result contains a lone surrogate — `encodeURIComponent()` throws `URIError: URI malformed`, JSON serialisers may reject the string, and downstream display surfaces render broken characters.

The codebase already applies `truncateUtf16Safe` / `sliceUtf16Safe` in 30+ locations (#98644, #102470, #101728, #104800, etc.). These two truncation sites were missed.

## Why This Change Was Made

`normalizeCliContextValue` truncates session_id/run_id for error message formatting in `formatCliOutputError`. `formatSkillExperienceReviewTranscript` truncates rendered LLM conversation output for skill review prompts. Both receive arbitrary Unicode content from users/models.

The fix follows the established pattern — replace raw `.slice(0, N)` with `truncateUtf16Safe`, and `full.slice(-tailBudget)` with `sliceUtf16Safe(full, tailStart)`. Same approach as #98644 (ZengWen-DT) and #102470 (zw-xysk).

## User Impact

- Error messages from `formatCliOutputError` no longer produce broken characters at emoji boundaries
- Skill experience review transcripts no longer corrupt emoji at truncation boundaries
- Affected strings survive `encodeURIComponent` / `JSON.stringify` / UTF-8 disk write without throwing

## Evidence

**Environment**: Node.js v24.13.1, @openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice, Linux x86_64, upstream/main at bd2be839c.

**Scenario 1 — normalizeCliContextValue** (CLI session_id straddling emoji at 200-char boundary):

```bash
node --import tsx -e '
import { truncateUtf16Safe } from "@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice";
const id = "s".repeat(199) + "😀tail";
const before = id.slice(0, 200);
const after  = truncateUtf16Safe(id, 200);
const last = (s) => JSON.stringify(s.slice(-5));
console.log("before:", last(before), "len:", before.length);
console.log("after:",  last(after),  "len:", after.length);
try { encodeURIComponent(before); console.log("encodeURIComponent(before): ok"); }
catch (e) { console.log("encodeURIComponent(before):", e.message); }
try { encodeURIComponent(after); console.log("encodeURIComponent(after): ok"); }
catch (e) { console.log("encodeURIComponent(after):", e.message); }
'
```

```
before: "ssss\ud83d" len: 200          ← lone high surrogate at end
after:  "sssss" len: 199               ← safely truncated before emoji
encodeURIComponent(before): URI malformed ← crashes
encodeURIComponent(after): ok             ← passes
```

**Scenario 2 — experience-review first message** (`.slice(0, 6000)` bisecting emoji):

```bash
node --import tsx -e '
import { truncateUtf16Safe } from "@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice";
const content = "[user]\n" + "a".repeat(5992) + "😀rest";
const before = content.slice(0, 6000);
const after  = truncateUtf16Safe(content, 6000);
const hasDangling = (s) => /[\uD800-\uDBFF](?![\uDC00-\uDFFF])|(?<![\uD800-\uDBFF])[\uDC00-\uDFFF]/u.test(s);
console.log("before len:", before.length, "dangling:", hasDangling(before), "tail:", JSON.stringify(before.slice(-2)));
console.log("after  len:", after.length,  "dangling:", hasDangling(after),  "tail:", JSON.stringify(after.slice(-2)));
'
```

```
before len: 6000 dangling: true tail: "a\ud83d"   ← lone high surrogate
after  len: 5999 dangling: false tail: "aa"       ← safe
```

**Scenario 3 — experience-review tail** (`.slice(-tailBudget)` starting at low surrogate):

```bash
node --import tsx -e '
import { sliceUtf16Safe } from "@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice";
const full = "a".repeat(10000) + "🦞" + "b".repeat(100);
const tailBudget = 101; const start = full.length - tailBudget;
const before = full.slice(-tailBudget);
const after  = sliceUtf16Safe(full, start);
const hasDangling = (s) => /[\uD800-\uDBFF](?![\uDC00-\uDFFF])|(?<![\uD800-\uDBFF])[\uDC00-\uDFFF]/u.test(s);
console.log("start:", start, "full[10000]:", JSON.stringify(full[10000]), "full[10001]:", JSON.stringify(full[10001]));
console.log("before first:", JSON.stringify(before[0]), "dangling:", hasDangling(before));
console.log("after  first:", JSON.stringify(after[0]),  "dangling:", hasDangling(after));
'
```

```
start: 10001 full[10000]: "\ud83e" full[10001]: "\udd9e"  ← 🦞 spans [10000]-[10001]
before first: "\udd9e" dangling: true                      ← starts with lone low surrogate
after  first: "b"      dangling: false                     ← aligned ✅
```

